{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers","id":1124633,"title":"[2E] Vampires Nightmare vs werewolves Kuruth Triggers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-03T23:21:38-07:00","id":1124633,"title":"[2E] Vampires Nightmare vs werewolves Kuruth Triggers","content":"It's crossover question, so I putted it in general <b>CoD</b> forum. I have story about Tribes of Moon werewolves uncovering Nosferatu vampires infested monastery. When looking over Disciplines of Nosferatu, I uncovered that vampiric power can make target thinks he's greatest fears are coming true ( just see Face of the Beast, The Grand Delusion or Waking Nightmare ). Those things for Uratha are mostly their Kuruth Triggers - probably even those most specific ones. <b>Can vampires Nightmare Discipline trigger Kuruth in werewolves target?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T23:27:46-07:00","id":1124635,"title":"","content":"They could, at least some could, since they involve some mind control. Face of the Beast 'merely' amplifies an existing fear, which wouldn't really matter. The Grand Delusion makes something seem like it's really happening, which would fit, but the vampire cannot 'inspire a delusion that would make the victim homicidal or self-destructive.' So that's out. You could have a Devotion that does it, though, a dot higher or so, or you could just ignore that aspect of the Discipline. Waking Nightmare makes a hallucination that could trigger werewolves with the Other trigger set, or the Territory one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:10:40-07:00","id":1124702,"title":"","content":"No, Nightmare would not trigger Kuruth for two reasons. Nightmare triggers fear only, not anger. Death Rage is, well, rage. Nightmare does not, at the base level, cannot trigger the emotions to cause a rage of any kind. That's not what it does.<br /> <br /> The second reason? Kuruth has some very specific triggers - Spending too long in Gauru. Taking Gauru outside of combat. Taking damage from silver. Forced into Kuruth by an Elodoth. One category of the player's choice, listed on page 103: Moon, Other, Pack, Territory, Wounds. Of the personal trigger options, only Other really could possibly count as a trigger here (facing a non-mortal, non-werewolf), and that's the result of knowing you're facing a vampire, which has nothing to do with the Discipline. Hells, given the nature of Disciplines, the werewolf can't even realize he's faced with an Other at this point if he didn't already (Wolves and vamps tend to recognize each other on sight, but Nosferatu tend to have Obfuscate and hide themselves). Anyways, my point is that the Other Trigger (if that was taken) should have happened a lot earlier or after the Discipline wears off and the werewolf puts two and two together, depending on the presence of Obfuscate or not. <br /> <br /> In short, there is nothing about the nature of Kuruth that should go off from being hit by Nightmare, and there is no reason for Nightmare to trigger a Rage. <br /> <br /> Disclaimer - I'm talking about Werewolf 2e. Werewolf 1e had a &quot;fear rage&quot; that just involved running away, which is appropriate. 2e does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:48:24-07:00","id":1124715,"title":"","content":"I think that for some triggers the nightmare could start the kuruth. E.g: see the moon is a trigger for some werewolfs, so this character could have fear to see the moon and lost control, then in this case it is a fear and the nightmare could trigger this fear as kuruth trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:57:11-07:00","id":1124719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124702#post1124702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, there is nothing about the nature of Kuruth that should go off from being hit by Nightmare, and there is no reason for Nightmare to trigger a Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that triggers are not fear-based, it's worth noting that the Nightmare discipline is not just 'feel fear.'<br /> <br /> Take a note of Waking Nightmare, which is fear-tainted, but otherwise just an illusion.<br /> <br /> 'This terrible hallucination manifests to all senses, though it generally can\u2019t change more than a single person, object, or feature of the location. She could invert the colors in a building, create a shambling monster that stalks her victims, or give herself a nightmarish appearance. The Storyteller should work with the player to determine how big a change the vampire can make. Once created, the Nosferatu can control how the vision reacts while it remains in her presence; once she has separated from her victims, her creation takes on a life of its own.'<br /> <br /> This is the Exceptional Success condition, and it would be understandable if the standard Success was assumed not to 'manifest to all senses.' But the vampire would effectively be making an illusion of something to the werewolf. I don't believe you would be able to trick a werewolf into believing they've been struck by silver with it, but one of the triggers is seeing your auspice moon in the sky, or seeing a werewolf you don't know in your territory. These would require specific information from the vampire which would be hard to find, except maybe with Auspex, but I think a vampire could conceivably trigger a werewolf if the Uratha had the right triggers, the vampire had the right Disciplines and knew of those triggers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:01:16-07:00","id":1124721,"title":"","content":"Why would the vampire -want- to trigger Kuruth though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:07:51-07:00","id":1124725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124721#post1124721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the vampire -want- to trigger Kuruth though?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the werewolf is talking to some of its vampire allies making it rage could ruin their relationship.<br /> <br /> But that's a stretch. Unless your Harmony is way out there you're going to have some control over your rage and be able to duck out, even if you don't have one of the many abilities that allows you to stave off rage. Then there's the fact that you might just be able to get confirmation, 'We had a full moon last week,' and realize you're being influenced.<br /> <br /> It's not the kind of thing you want to do when you're confronting them in combat but for other manipulation or screwing around stuff it's okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:27:14-07:00","id":1124729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124715#post1124715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for some triggers the nightmare could start the kuruth. E.g: see the moon is a trigger for some werewolfs, so this character could have fear to see the moon and lost control, then in this case it is a fear and the nightmare could trigger this fear as kuruth trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I think - Triggers are things werewolves ARE AFRAID cause under them they lose control - and can slaughter dozens of humans with their Pack, when Kuruth is spreading. Triggers are weakneses of Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:30:29-07:00","id":1124731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124721#post1124721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the vampire -want- to trigger Kuruth though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mindless beast is much easier to control, in the end. Just give Raging werewolf something to kill - and he will run to it. Sent some humans beside you and Uratha, and he will slaughter them - not you. You even can get later support from families of dead humans to 'slay the wolf'. \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:34:54-07:00","id":1124733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124729#post1124729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly what I think - Triggers are things werewolves ARE AFRAID cause under them they lose control - and can slaughter dozens of humans with their Pack, when Kuruth is spreading. Triggers are weakneses of Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the wrong way to look at it. Not all werewolves are going to fear going to rage, at Harmony 6-7 and 3-4 you have between 1 and 5 minutes of soft rage to compose yourself. At 5 you don't even have those triggers. And even if they did, being afraid of it isn't a trigger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124731#post1124731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mindless beast is much easier to control, in the end. Just give Raging werewolf something to kill - and he will run to it. Sent some humans beside you and Uratha, and he will slaughter them - not you. You even can get later support from families of dead humans to 'slay the wolf'. \ud83d\ude08</div> </div> </div> </div>The point was that the vampire who used Nightmare would likely be on the list of 'something to kill'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:52:16-07:00","id":1124772,"title":"","content":"Actually under the right circumstance; nightmare 2 will trigger Kuruth. Read the Frightened Condition in Requiem. <br /> <br /> Then we start a lot of if. If the trigger is right, and the Nosfartu knows or successfully guesses the right hallucination, Nightmare 4 should also trigger Kuruth. Rage after all is more then often sourced in fear. As explained a lot better by people above.<br /> <br /> And every single noticebly supernatural power will trigger Kuruth if the werewolf has the trigger form that and is unbalanced.<br /> <br /> Also, the go to power for fucking up people with rage is Animalism 4, that does trigger Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:58:41-07:00","id":1124776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124733#post1124733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point was that the vampire who used Nightmare would likely be on the list of 'something to kill'</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one of the nosfarus in the &quot;infested monastary&quot; is likely to have obfuscate 3. Good luck for werewolves to see through obfuscate. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:10:32-07:00","id":1124783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124776#post1124776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least one of the nosfarus in the &quot;infested monastary&quot; is likely to have obfuscate 3. Good luck for werewolves to see through obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does it cover all five senses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:50:19-07:00","id":1124798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124783#post1124783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Does it cover all five senses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it does","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:35:48-07:00","id":1124807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124776#post1124776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least one of the nosfarus in the &quot;infested monastary&quot; is likely to have obfuscate 3. Good luck for werewolves to see through obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank goodness Impossible Spoor costs just 1xp to get. The metaphorical shadows that cloak you literally give you away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:42:58-07:00","id":1124811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124772#post1124772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually under the right circumstance; nightmare 2 will trigger Kuruth. Read the Frightened Condition in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes you run away from something, it would do the opposite of Kuruth. You would shift to wolf form for better speed. Rage may be sourced in fear, but Kuruth is not just rage.<br /> <br /> Just being afraid, even magically afraid, isn't a Kuruth Trigger. You can customize one for it but that's obviously a special circumstance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And every single noticebly supernatural power will trigger Kuruth if the werewolf has the trigger form that and is unbalanced. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Other trigger would activate with the presence of vampires if they were strongly unbalanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124798#post1124798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes it does</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of.<br /> <br /> 'He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.' This is enough to start tracking, as Malus points out Impossible Spoor is pretty much made for that.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd there's a whole swathe of other abilities that would cause a Clash of Wills and shatter it, like Scent of the Unknown and Lore of the Land or Boundary Ward. Plus you can just find them through Tracking, which obviously werewolves have an advantage with. We've gone over this in the vampire forum.<br /> <br /> Or you could just breathe fire across the area you think they're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:05:03-07:00","id":1124866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124811#post1124811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just breathe fire across the area you think they're in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fire - the solution to many of life's problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:11:54-07:00","id":1124869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124866#post1124866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, fire - the solution to many of life's problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we saw the spoilers, before the book even came out, and found it's been an option, it's been one of my favorite ideas for Forsaken. The fire breathing werewolf. Useful against just about everything they come across, especially the dead and swarms. I'd be surprised that no one ever brings it up happening in their games but people don't talk about their games much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:23:06-07:00","id":1124874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124807#post1124807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank goodness Impossible Spoor costs just 1xp to get. The metaphorical shadows that cloak you literally give you away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible Spoor makes your successful Tracking rolls more successful and lets you spend Essence to stop penalties representing the trail getting cold over time from affecting them, neither of which actually cuts through the mental block of don't-notice-this that Obfuscate deals in \u2014 the Facet doesn't interact with any of the other penalties on the relevant chart, including &quot;Prey leaves unusually strong/weak trail,&quot; which is the closest translation to what the Discipline inflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:30:26-07:00","id":1124881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124874#post1124874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Impossible Spoor makes your successful Tracking rolls more successful and lets you spend Essence to stop penalties representing the trail getting cold over time from affecting them, neither of which actually cuts through the mental block of don't-notice-this that Obfuscate deals in \u2014 the Facet doesn't interact with any of the other penalties on the relevant chart, including &quot;Prey leaves unusually strong/weak trail,&quot; which is the closest translation to what the Discipline inflicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible Spoor adds 2 to successful Tracking rolls. Since Tracking rolls against Obfuscated vampires work against their Obfuscate and potentially other issues, it's still an advantage.<br /> <br /> 'The vampire can be tracked by indirect clues, as mentioned above. Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate. Teamwork may be applied.'<br /> <br /> Alone it won't 'break' Obfuscate but it goes a good way towards helping a werewolf overcome it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:36:45-07:00","id":1124888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124869#post1124869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since we saw the spoilers, before the book even came out, and found it's been an option, it's been one of my favorite ideas for Forsaken. The fire breathing werewolf. Useful against just about everything they come across, especially the dead and swarms. I'd be surprised that no one ever brings it up happening in their games but people don't talk about their games much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tongue of Fire Facet of the Gift of Elements? I thought it was being poetic with the name, but that is one way to interpret Influence: Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:38:08-07:00","id":1124890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124702#post1124702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Nightmare would not trigger Kuruth for two reasons. Nightmare triggers fear only, not anger. Death Rage is, well, rage. Nightmare does not, at the base level, cannot trigger the emotions to cause a rage of any kind. That's not what it does.<br /> <br /> The second reason? Kuruth has some very specific triggers - Spending too long in Gauru. Taking Gauru outside of combat. Taking damage from silver. Forced into Kuruth by an Elodoth. One category of the player's choice, listed on page 103: Moon, Other, Pack, Territory, Wounds. Of the personal trigger options, only Other really could possibly count as a trigger here (facing a non-mortal, non-werewolf), and that's the result of knowing you're facing a vampire, which has nothing to do with the Discipline. Hells, given the nature of Disciplines, the werewolf can't even realize he's faced with an Other at this point if he didn't already (Wolves and vamps tend to recognize each other on sight, but Nosferatu tend to have Obfuscate and hide themselves). Anyways, my point is that the Other Trigger (if that was taken) should have happened a lot earlier or after the Discipline wears off and the werewolf puts two and two together, depending on the presence of Obfuscate or not. <br /> <br /> In short, there is nothing about the nature of Kuruth that should go off from being hit by Nightmare, and there is no reason for Nightmare to trigger a Rage. <br /> <br /> Disclaimer - I'm talking about Werewolf 2e. Werewolf 1e had a &amp;quot;fear rage&amp;quot; that just involved running away, which is appropriate. 2e does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good answer. I find myself agreeing, though I would add that in theory, some werewolves might fear Kuruth itself, and by extension, their own triggers for it.<br /> <br /> I also wonder what would happen if an obfuscated Nosferatu used The Grand Delusion to make a werewolf with The Other trigger think a random passerby was a non-human, non-werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:42:09-07:00","id":1124894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124888#post1124888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tongue of Fire Facet of the Gift of Elements? I thought it was being poetic with the name, but that is one way to interpret Influence: Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just shoot it out of your hands or make it appear at will. But why would you?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://img06.deviantart.net/d539/i/2013/243/d/b/deerstalker_by_alradeck-d6kgbv9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://www.artofmtg.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Smoldering-Werewolf-Eldritch-Moon-MtG-Art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:05:39-07:00","id":1124906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124881#post1124881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Impossible Spoor adds 2 to successful Tracking rolls. Since Tracking rolls against Obfuscated vampires work against their Obfuscate and potentially other issues, it's still an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an advantage that doesn't actually increase your odds of success, is the thing \u2014 extra successes can account for some of the lost time a penalty would indirectly cause, but losing dice on the roll means you just change the minimum difference in progress from zero or one to zero or three.<br /> <br /> There's also the difference of systems to account for; Impossible Spoor is written to interact with Werewolf's core Tracking mechanics, both versions of which work differently from Vampire's roll to track an Obfuscated vampire. It might just come down to a Clash roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:37:54-07:00","id":1124950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124721#post1124721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the vampire -want- to trigger Kuruth though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Number one reason I come up with are variations of the idea it turns the werewolf into a bomb of carnage to those around him that he can perceive, which may not include an invisible vampire. There are many variation of where that'd be handy, but how vampire knows which fear-tainted illusion button to poke is where the questions get tricky.<br /> <br /> How would the vampire possibly know?<br /> I mean it is possible for them to know, or more likely <i>suspect</i>, but assured accurate intelligence of that nature is uncommon to say the least among vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:46:43-07:00","id":1125019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124811#post1124811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes you run away from something, it would do the opposite of Kuruth. You would shift to wolf form for better speed. Rage may be sourced in fear, but Kuruth is not just rage.<br /> <br /> Just being afraid, even magically afraid, isn't a Kuruth Trigger. You can customize one for it but that's obviously a special circumstance.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said, under certain conditions, nightmare 2 will trigger Kuruth. That is; if the wolf can't flee the source of fear, she will rage. Otherwise, you're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:59:20-07:00","id":1125025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1125019#post1125019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is; if the wolf can't flee the source of fear, she will rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're getting this part, though. Being afraid of things isn't a trigger to Kuruth. At the most you would shift to fight or run away and from the wording of the Discipline it seems getting away would be the priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T01:53:24-07:00","id":1125139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1125025#post1125025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure where you're getting this part, though. Being afraid of things isn't a trigger to Kuruth. At the most you would shift to fight or run away and from the wording of the Discipline it seems getting away would be the priority.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Im am getting it, you need to read up on the Frightened Condition, which the level 2 nightmare gives the subject. But im gonna quote the relevant part, from page 304 Requiem corebook 2ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can\u2019t approach the source of your fear or act<br /> against it \u2014 and if the only way out involves going near the<br /> source of your fear, you\u2019ll collapse on the ground in terror.<br /> Supernatural creatures prone to loss of control, including<br /> vampires, must roll to avoid frenzy. </div> </div> </div>If that isn't supposed to trigger Kuruth, I'm not sure anything will. It's as clear as day.<br /> And to be clear, under the right circumstance, it will trigger Kuruth. Being unable to flee, is that circumstance, as pointed out time and time again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 08-05-2017, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:36:39-07:00","id":1125178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1124633-2e-vampires-nightmare-vs-werewolves-kuruth-triggers?p=1124906#post1124906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the difference of systems to account for; Impossible Spoor is written to interact with Werewolf's core Tracking mechanics, both versions of which work differently from Vampire's roll to track an Obfuscated vampire. It might just come down to a Clash roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best option, in my opinion. Obfuscate 3 specifically allows tracking. Impossible Spoor aids tracking. This is a clear example of two powers clashing with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}